items.description:
Web browsers (Chrome, Safari) automatically suspend AudioContext after a period of inactivity or when the tab is backgrounded. playTone() checks if audioCtx exists but does not check audioCtx.state or call audioCtx.resume() before scheduling nodes. If the context is suspended, no sound plays and no error is shown.

File: web/src/main.js, playTone() ~line 130

Reproduction: Create AudioContext on first key, leave tab in background 30+ seconds, return and press a key — no sound.

Fix: At the top of playTone(), add:
  if (audioCtx.state === 'suspended') {
    audioCtx.resume().then(() => playTone(freq));
    return;
  }
OR schedule after resume():
  audioCtx.resume().then(() => { /* schedule oscillator */ })
